# No automated browser / web checks (default)

Agents must **not** use **Browserbase** (`user-browserbase`), **Cursor IDE Browser** MCP, **Browse** plugins, or any other **browser automation** or **live web smoke tests** to verify deployments, dashboards, or production URLs.

This applies to **routine post-change verification**, **QA passes**, and **“check that the page loads”** style tasks.

## What to do instead

- **`npm run typecheck`** and **`npm run deploy`** when the change ships.
- **Code review** of `public/**`, `src/dashboard/**`, and related assets.
- **D1 / Observability / logs** when debugging runtime behavior (per other project rules).
- **Ask the user** to sanity-check the UI in their browser if a visual confirmation is needed.

## Exception

Only if the **user explicitly asks** in that conversation for browser-based verification (e.g. “open the site in browser X and screenshot Y”), an agent may use the tooling the user named. Otherwise, **do not** spin up browser sessions or automated web checks.

## Secrets

Never paste dashboard passwords, API keys, or automation session secrets into chat or committed files.
